      "prompt": "Which statement correctly identifies the container holding the most sand?",
      "choices": [
        "Container 1, the square prism, because 120 in³ exceeds both other volumes.",
        "Container 2, the cylinder, because about 117.8 in³ exceeds both other volumes.",
        "Container 3, the cone, with a volume of about 125.2 in³.",
        "All three containers have the same volume, 120 in³."
      ],
      "answerIndex": 2,
      "explanation": "Container 1: 4²(7.5) = 120 in³. Container 2: π(2.5²)(6) ≈ 117.8 in³. Container 3: (1/3)π(3.75²)(8.5) ≈ 125.2 in³. Container 3 has the greatest volume."
